FAQ = [
 ("What is the best trailer hitch for a 2020–2026 Highlander?",
  "For most non-XSE owners, the CURT 13460. It is a 2 in Class 3 hitch rated 6,000 lb gross trailer weight and 900 lb tongue weight, and up to 8,000 lb with weight distribution, with a limited lifetime warranty. etrailer sells it as C45CR for $256.62 and lists it as hybrid compatible. XSE owners should look at the B&W RH670220BW instead, because CURT excludes the XSE."),
 ("How much can a 2020–2026 Highlander tow?",
  "Gas Highlanders are rated 5,000 lb and Hybrids 3,500 lb. A Toyota dealer's 2025 guide lists 5,000 lb for the 2.4L turbo and 3,500 lb for the 2.5L hybrid. The 2020–2022 V6 models are also commonly listed at 5,000 lb; confirm in your owner's manual. A hitch rated 6,000 lb does not raise either number. The lower of the hitch and vehicle rating is always your limit."),
 ("Why do some hitches exclude the Highlander XSE?",
  "The XSE, added for 2021, has a different rear fascia and exhaust with twin tips, and some hitch brackets don't clear it. CURT lists the 13460 for 2020–2026 Highlanders excluding XSE. Reese lists its 84439 for 2014–2023 Highlanders excluding 2020–2023 models with twin-tip exhaust. etrailer lists the B&W BW62PR for both 2021–2026 non-XSE and XSE, so it is the one to check first on an XSE."),
 ("Will a hitch fit the Highlander Hybrid?",
  "Usually, yes. The Hybrid shares the body and frame rails with the gas model. etrailer marks the CURT C45CR (13460) and its own e75ZR as hybrid compatible, and B&W's BW62PR is listed without a hybrid exclusion. The difference is the tow rating: 3,500 lb for the Hybrid against 5,000 lb for gas models. A hitch rated 5,000 or 6,000 lb doesn't change that."),
 ("Does a hitch affect the Highlander's spare tire?",
  "Yes, and it's the gotcha most listings skip. etrailer's notes for every 2023 Highlander hitch it sells say it fits with the 18 in spare only, and that a larger spare can't be stored underneath with a hitch installed. etrailer also flags that owners with a 20 in full-size spare should verify compatibility on the B&W. If you replaced the spare with a 20 in wheel, plan where it goes before buying."),
 ("Do Grand Highlander hitches fit a regular Highlander?",
  "No. The Grand Highlander is a longer, wider, taller vehicle introduced in 2023, and it uses its own hitches, such as Draw-Tite 76639, which is listed for the 2024 Grand Highlander. Only buy hitches listed for the 2020–2026 Highlander. The one crossover is wiring: the Tekonsha T-One 118827 harness is listed for both the 2020–2025 Highlander and the 2024–2025 Grand Highlander."),
 ("Which wiring harness does a 2020+ Highlander need?",
  "The Tekonsha T-One 118827 is a plug-in 4-way flat T-connector listed for 2020–2025 Highlanders. It plugs in behind the taillight with no cutting or splicing, includes a circuit-protected ModuLite HD module, and Tekonsha quotes 30 minutes. Some other harness listings say a factory tow package is required. Tekonsha's page doesn't mention that, but confirm with the seller that your Highlander has the connector the harness plugs into."),
 ("Can I use a hanging bike rack on a CURT Highlander hitch?",
  "Not the vertical kind. CURT states the 13460 is not compatible with vertical hanging bike racks, which carry bikes hung by the front wheel. Platform and horizontal hanging racks are unaffected. The same note appears on other CURT SUV hitches. If you already own a vertical rack, check the B&W or Reese listing for a similar restriction before you buy."),
 ("Is a Class IV hitch worth it on a Highlander?",
  "Only for margin. The Reese 84439 is Class IV, rated 6,000 lb and 900 lb, and up to 8,000 lb with weight distribution, the same numbers CURT publishes for its Class 3 13460. Neither lets a Highlander tow above 5,000 lb. What the class really tells you is the receiver's build and rating; on this vehicle, fitment for your trim and exhaust matters more than class."),
 ("Will a hitch interfere with the hands-free liftgate?",
  "It can. etrailer's notes for the CURT C45CR on the Highlander say it may limit the hands-free liftgate. The kick sensor sits under the rear bumper, and a receiver right below it can get in the way of the kick motion. If you use that feature every day, check the install notes for the hitch you choose, and expect to kick slightly to one side."),
]

